Z||000002||sqoach||02-10-2001||06:57 PM||||i have a question. sorry this isn't helping you out any mike.<BR>from what i read, coilovers are struts that have modified springs that fit tightly over the strut? i found a new set of struts the other day, so i might want to get "coil overs" if that's what they are. i'm just trying to find a way to get a wider wheel in there. the stock springs are too big and stick out, making it hard to do much. i mentioned this to someone before and got a good picture of one installed. it was exactly what i needed.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||02-10-2001||10:12 PM||||Good to hear you got them. I also want to extend a huge Thank You to Jeff for getting them for us. I havent gotten mine yet, I dont think. I had them sent down to the store, and it never occured to me to have a look to see if they were there yet. Mine are the same kit you got, for modified bodies. I am going to let some one else answer the above question because frankly I am pretty stupid when it comes to this subject. I wanted them because they look really nice, allow me to lower the car and allow for better spring rate, and for about the same cost as a pair of lowering springs.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
