Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||02-11-2001||01:25 AM||||I put ground controls on my car about 8 months ago and love them!! Their on my koni struts. I didn't like the kit that ground control sent me , so I sent it back. The sleeve itself didn't fit snug on the strut. i measured the diamete of the strut and had them sent me a unit that would fit. I also had a new collar put on the strut as the sleeve didn't sit perfectly on the strut. i don't know how hard you guys drive your car , but another guy I run track events with got the "fiero kit" and put it on his koni's , long story short after a while the stress split the sleeve , The car dropped and made a mess of the car. <P><BR>What spring rates did you go for? ((mrfiero))<BR>I got 2 sets of springs 1st set from groundcontrol 2nd froma  wholesaler. 340lbs , and a 400lbs set (for engine conversion) I don't know if I need the 400lbs set since I already run modified Koni's..We will see though<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||02-11-2001||02:56 AM||||Jonathan,<P>I ordered 300# springs......I really have no idea if it's the right rate for me.....we'll have to wait and see.<P>Do you have any pics or instructions on how these things go together?  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Slammed Fiero||02-11-2001||03:24 AM||||No pics or instructions ,yet.... I can get you pics , the installis fairly easy. You may have to grind the collar on the strut down a bit for the sleeve to fit over. This is at the top of the strut body itself. My friend notched his collars to fit flat on the perch. 300 is a good rate for the street. My car rides too hard for permanent street duty. I will see if I can't get you some pics in the next week.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||FIEROCIOUS||02-11-2001||02:01 PM||||300lb springs is what I used and they are the perfect rate!||||reg||1
