Z||000015||FieroLT1||02-22-2001||10:03 AM||||Finally got mine last week. Thanks Jeff! I modified my KYBs to perfection only to find out that the sleeve does not fit snug over them. The sleeve is exactly 1/16" bigger. The strut is 2". Also, I can't figure out what keeps the aluminum coil top hat from moving around. What to do? I do not want to wait another three months for Hypnotise to help with the problem. Any ideas? <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>OK......the struts are already modified (perch cut off).  The threaded sleeve slides over it with no problems, but what is it supposed to perch on?  It slides all the way to the bottom......there appears to be nothing around to support the sleeve. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR> <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||rockcrawl||02-22-2001||04:43 PM||||Depending on the manufacturer, the sleeves don't always fit tightly. I've had some that fit so tight that I had to do a lot of filing and hammer them on, and others that had 1/8" gap. In the past I have wrapped the strut body with electrical tape to prevent the sleeve from rattling around. The sleeve should just sit against the bottom mount of the strut. Nothing really holds it in place except the weight of the car.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Wade87GT||02-22-2001||06:11 PM||||I've got the RCC setup (pre-made). Check out the pics from this thread. They might help<P>Wade||||reg||1
